<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - see Disposition_Stage__c.field-meta.xml
        in this folder for why a comment above the root breaks `sf` deploy at conversion.

        2026-08-21 - NEW FIELD (design doc agent-output/bov-scoring-and-selection.md, Item 2).
        Captured at Disposition Readiness - the very next stage is BOV Outreach, where each
        broker's BOV_Amount__c is compared against this number to compute the Value dimension of
        BOV_Submission__c.BOV_Score__c. No BOV score can be calculated until this is set.

        precision 18 / scale 0 matches Disposition__c.Accepted_Offer_Price__c on THIS SAME
        object, deliberately diverging from Property__c.Asking_Price__c (scale 2) - same-object
        consistency wins, and a sale price on this object is never quoted in cents.

        required=false, and MUST STAY false. 8 dispositions exist today with this blank; a
        required=true would refuse the very NEXT edit of every one of them. No validation rule
        requiring it either - see the 🔴 block below, this is not an oversight.

        🔴 KNOWN AND ACCEPTED (design Q-3) - THIS FIELD IS INVISIBLE AT THE 'BOV Outreach' STAGE.
        It is placed in the Details fieldSection (Facet-0a494558) on
        flexipages/Disposition_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml, and that section's own
        visibilityRule is STAGE gated: "Disposition_Stage__c NE 'BOV Outreach' AND NE
        'Active Listing' AND NE 'Closing' AND NE 'Sale Closes'". So the field is correctly
        editable at Disposition Readiness (where it is captured) but the whole section - and
        this field with it - disappears from the page at BOV Outreach, which is exactly the
        stage where an analyst reads the BOV scores this field feeds. The user has accepted this
        for now. THIS IS NOT A BUG - do not "fix" it by moving the field or widening the
        visibilityRule without re-confirming with the user first.

        ⚠ ALL 8 DISPOSITIONS THAT EXIST TODAY WILL HAVE THIS BLANK ON DEPLOY. Until an analyst
        backfills it on each one, every BOV_Submission__c row on every one of those 8
        dispositions loses the Value dimension of its BOV_Score__c entirely (the formula's guard
        returns null, not zero - see BOV_Submission__c/fields/BOV_Score__c.field-meta.xml once
        that field is converted to a formula in its own sequenced wave). The remedy is data
        entry, not code.

        🔴 DO NOT ADD A VALIDATION RULE REQUIRING THIS FIELD (design F-4 - answer is NO VR).
        DispositionApprovalAdvanceService writes the stage change off of Disposition Readiness
        via Database.update(..., AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE), which lifts CRUD/FLS but NEVER a
        validation rule - VALIDATION RULES STILL EVALUATE under SYSTEM_MODE. A VR here would
        fire on that stage-change save, refuse it, and leave Approval_Advance_Pending__c = true
        with NO error shown to the approver - a silently stranded approved disposition. The
        guard belongs in DispositionApprovalService.submitForApproval's STAGE_READINESS branch
        instead (developer-owned, tracked separately - not built by this change).

        2026-08-24 - RELABELED "Asking Price" -> "Expected Value". LABEL ONLY, everything above
        still applies unchanged: fullName stays Asking_Price__c (referenced by
        BOV_Score__c's formula as Disposition__r.Asking_Price__c, by DispositionApprovalService's
        submission guard, by DispositionSelector, and by layouts - none of those touched). The
        description and inlineHelpText below were reworded to say "expected value" instead of
        "asking price" / "list price" so they stay consistent with the new on-screen label;
        DispositionApprovalService.ASKING_PRICE_REQUIRED_MESSAGE was updated the same way (see
        that class - constant name unchanged, only the message text). Property__c.Asking_Price__c
        and Opportunity.Asking_Price__c are a DIFFERENT module (acquisitions) and were left alone.
    -->
    <fullName>Asking_Price__c</fullName>
    <description>Expected value for this sale (formerly labeled "Asking Price"; API name unchanged), captured at Disposition Readiness. Feeds BOV_Submission__c.BOV_Score__c's value dimension; a blank or zero value makes every BOV score on this sale blank.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>The expected value this sale is being marketed at. Enter it here during Disposition Readiness - this field lives only on this page at this stage and will not be shown after the sale advances, including at BOV Outreach where BOV scores are reviewed.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Expected Value</label>
    <precision>18</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>0</scale>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Currency</type>
</CustomField>
